-- Row il-75. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: the instruments, the places, the printed texts, the pointers, the dates and the commencement the two items read; item I1 first, then item I2.
-- Tests of the controls are in pf75-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings are in pf75-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose (two, one per item) are in pf75-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (revision 3027431; UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[shNNNN-pPPPP]` lines quote the Hebrew printed on the deposited image of Sefer HaChukim (SH) issue NNNN, printed page PPPP (registers/source-bundle/pages/). `ext:[kt10016-p2148]` quotes the printed issue of Kovetz HaTakanot (KT) 10016. These are official instruments (KT: the printed issue as archived on olaw.org.il, an archive not run by the State).
-- One `ext:` line is a CONSOLIDATION-ONLY quotation, tagged so: the consolidation's line for the definition, without the editors' bracketed note, which is not carried.
-- Every Hebrew string typed below is a stretch of the ext: line above it, and tools/hebcheck.py checks that each Hebrew run of this module is in the excerpt or on an ext: line.
-- Where the page prints a footnote number beside a word, the ext: line leaves the number out.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.

§ `References`

